WEBVTT

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.240
Mahiro-chan, be sure to drink 
your tea before it gets cold.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.080
Thanks.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.240
I'll drink it once I'm 
done with this system check.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:22.250
Speaking of, when was the last 
time you updated your OS?

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.750
Update?

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.150
I see. So never, huh?

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:37.440
Then I'll go ahead and download the 
newest—er... I'll make it all better again.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.270
If you don't mind, I'll connect it to my own 
PC so I can take care of it at any time.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:44.180
You're a lifesaver. Thanks.

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:46.270
I'm no good with mechas.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:47.990
Mecha...

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:51.900
Our grandfather calls PCs mechas too.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.790
So I'm about as modern as Karen-chan 
and Karin-chan's grandfather.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.410
Y-Yuko-senpai, cheer up!

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:03.240
There's nothing to feel down about.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.900
Japan has long followed the phrase, "the past has much to teach us."

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.980
And what a lovely phrase it is.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:12.730
There's no end to the new things 
one may learn from the old!

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:13.790
The old...

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.700
Mistress, you're making 
her feel even more down!

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.180
What have I done?

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.880
And now even our mistress is feeling down.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.440
Yayoi-chan, cheer up!

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.680
Yuko-senpai, you too!

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:32.730
Yuko-senpai, I think you're amazing 
for brewing tea this delicious.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:37.490
That's right! And you even make 
cute rice balls. It's amazing!

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:40.160
Right? You think so too, right, Yayoi-chan?

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.580
Y-Yes, but of course!

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:47.250
The food and treats Yuko-senpai makes are 
loved by the entire dormitory and beyond!

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.180
Thanks, everyone.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.930
The cookies I'm baking in the 
cafeteria should be about done now.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.300
I'll go get them.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:58.070
Oh, Yuko-senpai.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:01:59.300
What is it?

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.300
Yuko

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.300
Password Reset

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:02.300
Can you tell me your password?

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.640
Of course. It's 0617.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.580
0617?

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:11.770
It's my birthday. Easy to remember, right?

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.300
0617. Isn't that...

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.530
Today.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.610
Oh, you're right.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.370
No way!

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.490
How could we forget the birthday of 
the senpai we love and respect?!

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.490
How could she use such a dangerous password?!

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:26.230
Huh?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.310
This is no time to enjoy 
an elegant cup of tea!

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:08.660
Everyone, let's put our heads together and 
make Yuko-senpai's birthday party a success!

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:15.810
Goodness. Where are you all going?

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:19.280
Oh! Er... Um...

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.970
Sorry. We remembered we have some 
urgent business to attend to.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.030
Goodness gracious, that 
sounds like a handful.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.060
Right now the program's installing 
the best new software,

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.330
so don't touch anything please.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.330
Wait, Mahiro-chan. Take these.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.330
They're thanks for today.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:37.330
There's lots here, so 
share them with everyone.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.340
Yuko-senpai, I'll do my best!

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.340
S-Sure? Do your best.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:47.050
Meeting One to Strategize
for Yuko-Senpai's Birthday Party

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:55.880
Now then, I'd like to open our first meeting to 
strategize for Yuko-senpai's birthday party.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:05:00.320
As the class representative 
of our class, Class S,

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.020
I, Yayoi Tachibana,

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:04.940
will preside over this meeting and take 
responsibility to move our plan forward.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:10.910
I will devote my body and soul to making 
Yuko-senpai's birthday party a success!

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.210
Restart your computer to finish
installing important updates

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.210
mindows can't update important files 
and services while the system is using them.
Make sure to save your files before restarting.
Time until restart:

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.210
Postpone    Restart now

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.210
Remind me in: 10 minutes

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:16.610
First, we need to decide 
what kind of party we will have.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:19.210
Those of you with ideas, raise your hands now.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.710
Me, me, me!

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:22.340
I want to eat a big cake!

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:23.370
I want a high-end PC!

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:24.550
A Hamburg steak party!

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:25.760
Fluffy.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:30.680
Big cake
High end PC
Hotel dinner

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.680
Come on! Aren't you all just saying 
things that you want to do?

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:34.450
This is a party that's supposed 
to make Yuko-senpai feel happy.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:38.100
Then, how about a pajama party?

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:39.900
A pajama party?

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.370
A little while ago…

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:46.920
Goodness gracious.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:50.280
Ashley-chan said that she's going to have 
a pajama party tonight with her friends.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.280
A pajama party?

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:54.740
It's a sleepover.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:56.860
Everyone brings food and treats,

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:01.600
and has fun eating, 
playing games and chatting.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:03.300
Wow! It sounds so fun.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:05.530
It does.

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:10.050
I hope that one day, I can enjoy a pajama 
party with you and all of our friends.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.240
I see.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:14.740
If that's her wish, then we've 
no choice but to grant it.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.560
Why not make it a surprise party as well?

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:19.300
Yeah! I bet she'll be so happy!

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.620
Where shall we hold the party?

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:24.460
How about in the room Mahiro-chan and I share?

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:28.160
I think it would be difficult 
to clean up that room on time.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:33.860
And our room is a bit too cramped for 
everyone to relax and enjoy themselves in.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:37.700
A suite at a hotel might be the best choice.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.740
How about we just use Yuko-senpai's room?

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:42.990
When she opens the door to 
her room, she'll be shocked!

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:46.420
That's what I call a real 
surprise party! Or something?

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:48.300
I see.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.260
And if we decorate her room 
with balloons and sparkles,

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.930
I'm sure she'll be overjoyed!

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.390
Installing updates for your machine.
 Please do not power off or unplug your machine.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:02.900
By the way, have any of you ever 
gone to a pajama party before?

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:06.820
I don't even own a pair of pajamas.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.190
I just wear this to bed.

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:09.990
I'm the same. I generally 
sleep in monk's clothes.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:11.610
Same! I sleep buck naked!

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.520
Be careful not to catch a cold.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:15.480
What about you, Nina-chan?

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:18.600
Sorry.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:21.000
I don't do anything special
and just wear pajamas.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.000
<i>Hello, Yuko.</i>

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.840
Goodness. Hello, Mecha-san.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.050
Start preparations
Procure items
Shopping party departs for Pirari Town
Check party area
Start decorating for party
Finish decorating for party
Check party equipment area

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:32.400
I will take care of acquiring 
both the food and cake.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.740
I'd like everyone else to take 
care of decorating the party area.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:38.560
Now then, we've no time to spare.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.850
Let's get started on putting 
everything together!

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:41.720
Roger!

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:41.720
Understood.

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:42.820
Wait.

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:44.610
What's the matter?

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:46.860
What about the birthday present?

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.800
What have I done?! 
That's the most important part!

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:53.860
Mistress!

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:56.720
If it's all right with you, 
I'll go buy the present.

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:59.060
Since it's a pajama party,

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:01.370
why not make the present a pair of pajamas?

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:05.710
While I do think pajamas 
would make a good present…

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:08.960
Lion, you've never gone to 
Pirari Town before, have you?

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:10.550
Pirari Town?

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:22.560
<i>H-How can this be?!</i>

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:28.820
There's no way I can let her go alone!

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.820
I shall accompany you.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.660
I'll go too.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:37.570
I just received word that the book I had 
reserved has just arrived at the bookstore.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:41.690
Thanks! Oh, but all the decorating…

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:44.130
We'll be more than enough!

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:46.430
Leave everything over here to us.

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:48.670
Make sure to choose some beautiful pajamas.

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:50.160
Sure!

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:05.720
Be sure to choose lean meat 
over anything marbled with fat.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:08.630
I believe Yuko-senpai said 
she's on a diet right now,

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:12.050
so I think it's best to arrange a menu that's 
both low in calories and appealing to the eye.

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:38.660
Hey, what kind of place is Pirari Town?

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:41.510
It was built alongside the academy.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:45.220
That was back when my great, great 
grandfather was still young—

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:46.850
That's not what I mean!

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:49.170
There's a delicious ice cream parlor.

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:50.310
Yay!

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.290
And a taiyaki shop.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.340
Love it!

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:53.190
Buttered potatoes.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.420
My favorite!

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:55.450
Frankfurters.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:56.540
Let's go, let's go!

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.990
There are also cute variety stores.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:09:59.990
Yeah?

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.300
I see you're not very interested…

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:14.950
What's the matter?

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:18.050
Train gave me… motion sickness…

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.900
We have to get Yuko-senpai 
out of her room. And fast.

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:25.310
Are you two ready?

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:26.820
What are we going to do?

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:29.140
Yeah, I don't really have a plan.

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:32.680
We've got no choice now. 
We'll have to take her head on.

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:33.790
You mean?

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:35.510
Let's just ask her.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:39.450
We can say, "I can't tell you why, but we 
absolutely need you to leave right now!"

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:41.700
Even though it's her own room?

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.880
Yeah, that's kinda rash.

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:45.810
But we don't have any more time.

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:47.620
We have to do something.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.350
What are you doing?

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:54.170
I'm gonna get her to leave her room.

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:02.090
Come in.

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:03.670
Excuse me.

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:09.180
Today's an important day 
that comes but once a year.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:12.920
And to celebrate, I'll give you 
a day that you'll never forget.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:14.360
Yuko?

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:18.320
What's going on?

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:21.350
Yuko, what on earth have you done?

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:24.860
I have no idea. I didn't touch a thing.

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:27.370
It just keeps going crazy on its own.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:31.330
Would a PC just up and access secret 
information from ALCA on its own?!

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:35.590
This is bad! Bad!

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:36.870
Goodness gracious.

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:39.590
I'm going to go get Mahiro-chan so 
she can teach me how to stop it.

00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:45.350
Excuse us!

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:47.140
Coming through.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:50.770
<i>Hello, Yuko.</i>

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:54.000
You definitely chased 
Yuko-senpai out of her room,

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.260
but she'll be back right away.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:57.950
Yeah… About that…

00:11:57.950 --> 00:11:59.780
Thanks. You're a lifesaver.

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:03.710
Now I won't have to worry about Yuko being 
caught on the wrong side of the law.

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:05.780
I owe you guys one.

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:09.040
Then can you pay us back right now?

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.540
Buttered 
Potatoes

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:18.040
Obihiro Soft Serve

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:28.450
Lion-san, we didn't come here for sightseeing.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:30.350
What a cute bear!

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.310
Gosh.

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:34.560
Don't you think it's just 
perfect for Yuko-senpai?

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:39.270
Thanks for waiting.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:41.270
Oh, Nina-chan.

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:43.890
I want to give this to Yuko-senpai 
as a present. What do you think?

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:47.530
I think it would be perfect 
for a birthday when she's in her 60s.

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:50.730
I see. So it's still too early.

00:12:50.730 --> 00:12:53.280
Weren't we going to give 
her pajamas this time?

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:54.540
Where's the store?

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:59.240
It looks like there's one 
on the outskirts of town.

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:01.960
Stores around here close early

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:04.660
so it's about time we get moving, Lion-san.

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:09.750
I wonder where Mahiro-chan went.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:13.980
Goodness. What are you doing?

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:17.980
This room is currently off limits!

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:21.600
It turns out a bomb was found in this room.

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:23.380
Goodness gracious, that's terrible!

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:26.170
Didn't you hear the warning?

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:28.240
That was because it sensed a bomb was near!

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:30.760
I'll take you someplace safe.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:31.330
Come with me!

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:32.760
Goodness gracious.

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:36.940
Is she gone?

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:38.310
Yup!

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:44.330
Oh, speaking of, I took a 
pair of Senpai's old pajamas.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:48.930
We'll be safe all the way out here.

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:52.430
In any event, what are you doing tonight?

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:54.530
But I really wonder where everyone went.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:58.010
Do you fancy a chance to rendezvous under 
the stars, just the two of us, for a night out?

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:03.790
Huh? Huh?

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:08.200
Mahiro-chan? Lion-chan? Are you here?

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:11.200
What should I do?

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:14.200
Nobody's here, and it looks like 
I can't go back to my room.

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:16.700
At times like this…

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:18.460
it's time to clean!

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:26.090
Gate Access! Tetra-Heaven!

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.510
Vesta, will you lend me a hand?

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:35.640
<i>Of course. Let's have fun together, Yuko.</i>

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:03.360
This has been bothering me for a while.

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:05.780
Let's make it like new again!

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:22.890
Cleaning really heals the soul!

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:26.310
You're still eating?

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:31.860
What's the matter?

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:35.170
D-Don't cry. There there.

00:15:35.170 --> 00:15:36.480
I wonder if she's lost.

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:38.920
Hey, where's your mother?

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.120
We've got a problem on our hands.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:45.760
It's cute.

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:47.500
That was quick.

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:51.840
There's a flower I want, no matter what.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:54.600
But it's not blooming anywhere.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:55.940
What kind of flower is it?

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:58.850
It's pure white and really big.

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:01.170
It's a really pretty flower.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:05.480
It's about this big, and 
it smells really nice.

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:09.190
That's way too difficult to put together.

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:13.220
Maybe…

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:18.910
Dahlia? It's not in season 
yet, so we don't have any.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:20.880
That's too bad.

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:23.650
You don't want any other 
flower but a dahlia, right?

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:26.440
It's a present for someone 
really important to me.

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:29.670
Let's go visit some other stores.

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:38.640
I'm afraid not.

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:42.050
But Dahlia flowers sure are popular today.

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:44.280
There was another person looking 
for that flower today around noon.

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:48.240
Dahlia? We don't have any.

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:52.120
Oh, but we do have some seeds.

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:54.110
I'll take those!

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:57.460
And what do you plan on 
doing with those seeds?

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:05.850
Gate Access! Monolium!

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:10.840
Let's give it a try, Rosa!

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:13.720
<i>I understand how you feel.</i>

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:46.500
Thank you, miss!

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:51.300
Isn't that great?

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:51.890
Yes.

00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:52.980
It is.

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:55.270
Presents are important.

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:58.740
Wait, this is no time to be standing around!

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:01.010
We have to hurry and get to that store!

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:03.310
<b>Kuronuma's Bedding</b>

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:10.560
A birthday without a present?

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:14.610
This is more wretched than a shortcake 
without a strawberry on top.

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:16.500
We're done for.

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:19.350
Yayoi-chan, I'm really sorry.

00:18:19.350 --> 00:18:22.080
There's no need for you 
to apologize, Lion-san.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:26.040
To begin with, if I had remembered
Yuko-senpai's birthday,

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:28.540
I could have spent more time 
preparing things properly.

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.870
But you already have a present.

00:18:32.390 --> 00:18:34.800
A very special present.

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:58.600
What's this? Aren't these pajamas…

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:03.320
Invitation

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:03.320
Yuko-senpai, please come 
in your pajamas!

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:03.320
Goodness gracious, what could this be?

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:05.580
I'm looking forward to it.

00:19:11.590 --> 00:19:14.210
Did you find the invitation?

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:17.360
Yes. I'm really looking forward to it.

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:22.470
Tonight's sure to be a 
night you'll never forget.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.230
Happy birthday! Yuko-senpai

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:34.730
Yuko-senpai, happy birthday!

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:37.730
Goodness gracious, what shall I do?

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:41.530
Goodness gracious, when did you do all this?

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:45.330
This is from all of us.

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:47.870
Aren't they lovely?

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:50.870
In the language of flowers, 
white dahlias mean

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:52.500
thank you.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:53.370
There you have it.

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:57.950
This is the first time I've had 
such a wonderful birthday party.

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:12.310
Thank you, everyone.

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:15.580
I'll never forget today.

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:18.690
Yuko-senpai!

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:19.820
Goodness gracious.

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:25.470
Oh, by the way, here's a 
birthday present from me.

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:26.570
Thank you.

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:31.180
It's a perfect, unhackable password.

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:32.620
I leave it in your hands.

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:36.430
Goodness gracious. 
I wonder if I'll be able to handle it?

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:45.900
She just makes me do all the work.

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:47.660
Where did she go?

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:51.390
To my dear Kozue

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:54.740
Really, she's such a swindler.

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:08.950
That Yuko sure is late.

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:13.510
She's just so shy.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:19.040
Episode 4

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:19.040
Repay Kindness With Flowers

00:22:50.450 --> 00:22:53.020
And today was supposed to be my day off!

00:22:53.020 --> 00:22:56.200
Guess I'm stuck having drinks 
with you again, Senpai.

00:22:56.200 --> 00:22:59.120
How rude. That's my line.

00:22:59.120 --> 00:23:04.270
Oh, I heard Lion-san and her friends are all 
having a birthday party for Morigaya-san.

00:23:04.270 --> 00:23:07.030
Huh? I heard it was a pajama party.

00:23:07.350 --> 00:23:09.170
Whatever either way!

00:23:09.170 --> 00:23:13.380
Nothing good ever happens when 
I have a birthday party anymore!

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:24.670
Next episode

00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:16.330
I feel like I'll run out or 
breath before I get done

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:19.310
blowing out all the candles 
for every year on the cake!

00:23:19.310 --> 00:23:24.580
And a pajama party! It's like they're 
just showing off how good their life is.

00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:25.800
Rino, today,

00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:28.630
this flower suits you perfectly.

00:23:29.050 --> 00:23:30.940
A yellow rose?

00:23:30.940 --> 00:23:33.720
In the language of flowers, 
it means jealousy.

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:36.310
They say dumplings over flowers anyway!

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:39.120
Boss! Get me all the grilled mutton you can!
